               <p xml:id="idm115">On 28 July 1869 the Danish Crown Prince Frederik (later King Frederik VIII) was married in Stockholm to Princess Lovisa, daughter Carl XV of Sweden. On their return to Copenhagen a festive celebration on a grand scale was organized by the municipal government. It was held on 11 August in the gardens of Rosenborg Castle. Danmarksstøtten (The Denmark Statue) refers to a colossal statue representing Denmark made especially for the occasion by Vilhelm Bissen and Lauritz Prior. The song was later turned into a song for mixed choir and brass called "Vinterdage" (Winter Days) with a new text by Carl Andersen.</p>
            </history>
